# llm-scaler v52 (SPLITS engagement) — bake v1.2.5t3 -> v1.2.5t3b (TEST)
#
# t3b = t3 (TQ MQ split ladder default-32 + G2 env-only gate + crash-4
# fix A/B + v52b telemetry) + the R2 delivery root fix + R1 telemetry:
#
#   async_sched_v52.py  -> vllm/v1/core/sched/async_scheduler.py
#     (crash-4 R2 root fix: F8v2 force-finish now stashes the terminal
#      (client_index, finish_reason) at reap time; terminal
#      EngineCoreOutputs are merged into the next update_from_output
#      return or flushed at the engine idle transition — the reaped
#      client stream terminates instead of hanging forever. On t3 the
#      t07 repro showed the reaped request's HTTP client hang with the
#      engine idle: update_from_output only delivers finals for
#      requests in num_scheduled_tokens and never for is_finished()
#      ones, and non-DP async mode has no other delivery path — the
#      crash-3 "usage-less silent stream end", reproduced
#      2026-09-06 16:14.)
#
#   core_v52.py         -> vllm/v1/engine/core.py
#     (crash-4 R2 root fix: _v52_flush_pending_finishes() called at the
#      idle transition (before _notify_idle_state_callbacks) and on
#      steps that did not execute the model — the delivery path for
#      scheduler-finished-but-unscheduled requests in non-DP async
#      mode; getattr-guarded so non-v52 schedulers are unaffected.)
#
#   gpu_model_runner_v52.py -> vllm/v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py
#     (crash-4 R1 root-cause TELEMETRY ONLY: v52c DISCARD-GAP logs the
#      worker-vs-scheduler token-count gap driving discard_request_mask,
#      once per (request, gap) episode — evidence for the zombie
#      trigger root fix (2048/APC-boundary hypothesis); no behavior
#      change.)
#
# Base-file md5 gates below pin the exact v1.2.4 content before overlay
# (TQ bde20892..., FA 50fa85ce..., SCH 73817db5..., ASCH 956c51ac...,
# CORE 1d1ced0d..., GMR f610bbd3... — CORE/GMR verified 2026-09-06,
# untouched by all earlier overlays).
